					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tkd7PZydfS-ww8yfV",
					"name": "Chitin (Tyranid Warrior)",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "DR 60, all locations. Weak Points 5 (as a Ravener's, matching framework.md's own figure for this tier): on a hit that fails to penetrate, roll 3d; 5 or less halves DR (30). Eye clusters run at DR 30 rather than 60.\n\nLore: A Tyranid's exoskeleton is grown, not worn: dense bio-ceramic chitin fused directly to the flesh beneath it, thickest on the largest bioforms and thin enough on a Termagant to be more like a swarm-trooper's flak jacket than real armour plate. Universal across Codex background and every piece of Black Library Tyranid fiction.\n\nDesign: Damage Resistance (B46, 5/level, all locations): natural DR bought directly on the body, per framework.md's explicit instruction that chitin is a character trait, not equipment. Each body-type lens overrides `levels`/`dr` to its own figure from framework.md's Tyranid anchor table; see that lens's own copy of this trait for its point cost.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 60,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "dr_bonus",
							"locations": [
								"all"
							],
							"amount": 60
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tEMR-6l44Uldl7b12",
					"name": "Synapse Creature (Warrior)",
					"reference": "B35",
					"local_notes": "Every friendly Tyranid organism within 16 yards automatically gains Synapse Discipline's benefit and has Synapse Dependence suppressed, for as long as this creature is alive, conscious, and itself linked (directly or through a closer synapse creature) to the Hive Mind. A Tyranid Warrior's own Synapse Dependence is never active while it is drawing on the wider Hive Mind this way.\n\nLore: Tyranid Warriors are the swarm's front-line officers precisely because they project this field: Codex background across editions names Warriors, alongside larger synapse-capable bioforms, as the link that keeps a local swarm fighting with purpose instead of degenerating into a feeding frenzy the instant a fight turns bad.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Advantage Delivered (a 10-point granted advantage, at +10% per point it is worth, B36: +100%); Area Effect at the 16-yard tier (+200%, B102); Always On (-40%, B113, it cannot be switched off); Emanation (-20%, B111, proximity only, no attack roll). Net: +100+200-40-20 = +240%. 10 x 3.4 = 34 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "meY0yxQkfWxaCqPO7",
							"name": "Advantage Delivered (grants Synapse Discipline, 10 pts)",
							"cost_adj": "+100%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mSXo5EK-etdEeEOMs",
							"name": "Area Effect, 16 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+200%"
						},
						{
							"id": "moGmBfvABpl8ndZct",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mJr0DM14WWnB5SSJP",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "t2qkTUjSsspw_mkO_",
					"name": "Shadow in the Warp (Tyranid Warrior)",
					"reference": "B35",
					"local_notes": "Any psyker within 16 yards suffers -3 to Psyniscience, Warp Sorcery-tagged skill rolls, and the Will roll to resist Perils of the Warp, and must make an immediate Fright Check the first time they come within range.\n\nLore: A Warrior's synapse role means it carries a heavier share of the Hive Mind's psychic mass than a lesser predator bioform, widening its Shadow in the Warp to match its synapse range.\n\nDesign: Affliction (B35) base 10; Disadvantage Delivered (+30%); Area Effect at the 16-yard tier (+200%, B102); Always On (-40%); Emanation (-20%); Accessibility (-20%). Net: +30+200-40-20-20 = +150%. 10 x 2.5 = 25 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"modifiers": [
						{
							"id": "meMuuRE3-yJShOV5n",
							"name": "Disadvantage Delivered (Warp-Deafened: -3 to psychic skill and Warp Empowerment-related rolls, plus an immediate Fright Check on first exposure, -30 pts)",
							"cost_adj": "30%"
						},
						{
							"id": "m7a9qNKaNR-1UTJM_",
							"name": "Area Effect, 16 yards",
							"cost_adj": "+200%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mPJ453zqdOSmYnD0R",
							"name": "Always On",
							"cost_adj": "-40%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mjfFw8_WFheqLhUJ3",
							"name": "Emanation",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						},
						{
							"id": "mw3tzVPYwrlv-Ae5b",
							"name": "Accessibility (only affects psykers and other warp-sensitive minds)",
							"cost_adj": "-20%"
						}
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "thsirg8qoh1Luoi03",
					"name": "Injury Tolerance (Damage Reduction)",
					"reference": "P53",
					"local_notes": "Divisor 2 (level = divisor): after DR and wounding multipliers, all injury is divided by 2 (round down, minimum 1 if anything penetrated).\n\nLore: A Warrior's redundant organs and dense muscle let it fight on through wounds. Large synapse-beasts and monsters shrug off wounds that would fell smaller creatures.\n\nDesign: Injury Tolerance (Damage Reduction) (GURPS Powers p. 53, 25 points per level, level = divisor): divisor 2 = 50 points. Gives the Warrior the bulk-and-redundant-organs toughness the lore describes on top of its chitin DR and extra HP.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"Tyranids"
					],
					"points_per_level": 25,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 2,
					"base_points": 0
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tad_9lUeccVO8AUz1",
			"name": "Devourer",
			"reference": "B61",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A heavier gun-arm that hurls squirming, burrowing worms deep into a wound at automatic-weapon speed, favoured by Tyranid Warriors and Hive Tyrants who want sustained close-range firepower rather than a single hard-hitting shot. Codex: Tyranids background places it a clear step above the Fleshborer/Spinefists family and roughly level with an Astra Militarum autogun in raw stopping power, made up for by its far higher rate of fire.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor (updated after flak went to DR 30, for the same reason as the Fleshborer above): \"Devourer | Boring worms: 5d(2) pi++.\" Innate Attack (Huge Pierce) (B61, 8/die) at 5 dice = 40, with Armor Divisor (2) (B102, +50%) and Rapid Fire (B108, RoF 8 is in the 8-15 bracket, +100%): net +150%, 40x2.5=100. Checked by exact dice distribution: 5d(2) pi++ averages 17.5 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 69.5% of the time and rounds to 0% against carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) or heavier — now a genuinely reliable threat to flak-armoured infantry per shot, well past the old 4d(2) figure's 33.6% and past even the framework's own autogun anchor (9% vs flak), matching a \"boring worms\" weapon meant to chew through soft armour outright; RoF 8 then stacks on top of that already-solid per-shot chance, making a Warrior's Devourer a serious threat to anything short of carapace. Handling: Acc 3 and 150/450 range, this project's own rifle-class estimate for a Warrior-scale gun-arm; Shots 12(20), a shorter, 20-second regrowth for the faster-cycling brood.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 100,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "WKJrIOw7rH0fuu6RQ",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "pi++",
						"base": "5d",
						"armor_divisor": 2
					},
					"accuracy": "3",
					"range": "150/450",
					"rate_of_fire": "8",
					"shots": "12(20)",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "ST-independent, fused to the arm. Shots regrow from the bearer's boring-worm glands over the listed time.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "skill",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Innate Attack"
							},
							"specialization": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Projectile"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "dx",
							"modifier": -4
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tMFhtJJClUzak2I97",
			"name": "Scything Talons",
			"reference": "B88",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A pair of long, chitinous cutting blades grown from the forearms — the single most common melee symbiote in the swarm, carried by everything from Genestealers to Hive Tyrants in one form or another. Codex: Tyranids background across editions treats scything talons as the baseline killing weapon: not the swarm's hardest-hitting blade, but reliable, always-on, and lethal against anything short of the heaviest personal armour.\n\nDesign: Framework.md's own anchor: \"Scything talons | sw+2d(2) cut.\" Built at a Tyranid Warrior's own ST 34 (sw 6d, framework's bioform table): Cutting Striker (B88, 7 points) with Armor Divisor (2) (B102, +50%) = 7x1.5=10.5, rounded to 11, for the bare sw+0(2) cut baseline the wielder's own ST already provides for free; the anchor's own +2d on top is bought separately as Innate Attack (Cut) (B61, 7/die) at 2 dice = 14, with Armor Divisor (2) (+50%) and Melee Attack, Reach C (B112, -30%): net +20%, 14x1.2=16.8, rounded to 17. Total 11+17=28. Checked by exact dice distribution at ST 34 (sw+2d(2) = 8d(2)): averages 28 and penetrates flak (DR 30, eff. 15) 99.6% of the time, carapace (DR 70, eff. 35) 6.1%, and rounds to 0% against Astartes plate (eff. 50) and Terminators — a real killer of unarmoured and flak-armoured targets and only a marginal threat to carapace and none to rigid plate, matching \"lethal against anything short of the heaviest personal armour\" without overstating it against carapace. (A Ravener at ST 32, 8d-1(2): flak 99.3%, carapace 3.9%.) Skill: Brawling, per framework.md's own weapon- skill table for natural close-combat weapons (power fist/lightning claws use the same skill).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Tyranids"
			],
			"base_points": 28,
			"weapons": [
				{
					"id": "wmeSU0HP4QFvBJgLB",
					"sv": 1,
					"damage": {
						"type": "cut",
						"st": "sw",
						"base": "2d",
						"armor_divisor": 2
					},
					"reach": "1",
					"parry": "0",
					"usage": "Standard",
					"usage_notes": "Written for a Tyranid Warrior-scale bearer (ST 34, sw 6d, giving a total of 8d(2) cut; a Ravener at ST 32, sw 6d-1, gets 8d-1(2)); rebuild the +2d Innate Attack component for any other bearer's own ST per this file's header note.",
					"defaults": [
						{
							"type": "dx",
